<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Geelong's big housing boom and the asbestos cement era are the same stretch of years. The Housing Commission's Norlane program peaked between 1951 and 1957 and had put up 2,464 houses by 1976, and <a href="/asbestos-removal-lara/">Corio</a> gained five estates of roughly 2,500 more from the late 1950s. Asbestos cement was standard residential building material from the mid-1940s until the late 1980s, so sheeting on a fence, an eaves lining or a garage wall from that era is worth checking before anyone puts a tool through it.</p><p>We don't hold a removal licence and we don't claim one. What we do is take samples and have them analysed, then put you in touch with licensed asbestos removalists working across Greater Geelong, the Bellarine Peninsula, the Surf Coast and Golden Plains. You contract with the removalist directly, and their WorkSafe Victoria licence number appears on every quote. If something has already been cracked or broken, call (03) 5550 4817 and start with <a href="/asbestos-testing-geelong/">a test</a> rather than a guess.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Geelong</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Geelong Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos testing and identification</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">You can't tell fibro from modern fibre cement by looking at it, and an older Geelong house often has three or four different materials in play. We take the samples and a NATA-accredited laboratory does the analysis, usually back within one to five business days.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos fence removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Old fibro boundary fences are the most common residential job in Geelong's northern suburbs, and a full fence line is well past what anyone is meant to take on unlicensed. The removal is carried out by licensed asbestos removalists we work with, and their WorkSafe Victoria licence number is on the quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Roof, shed and garage removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Super Six roofing, garage and shed cladding and eaves linings are the bigger jobs, and the ones where sheets must never be water-blasted, drilled, dry-swept or walked on. A licensed removalist prices the removal itself; whatever goes back on afterwards is something you arrange separately with a registered builder.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Disposal and where it can legally go</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Asbestos is reportable priority waste in Victoria and can only go to a landfill authorised to receive it, never into a general skip or a council hard-waste collection. In the whole Barwon region that means Drysdale, which takes small domestic loads only, so ring (03) 5251 2935 before you drive out.</p>
      </div>
</div>
